                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "NOT RECOMMENDED - it is simply a big pain in the A to play. The controls are super stiff and the enemies' have patterns that outright grief you by taking advantage of it. It is often unclear where you even are.\n\nIn normal play the game kills you by level 3 (out of 13) where the damaging starts because you only have four (4) points of health while a casual playthrough most likely involves over 100 hits. You know - in a roguelite meaning you can never heal. Also the overheating mechanic means you will take damage even when you are just moving around.\n\nThe default keyboard control scheme is clearly left-handed and it tends to default back to that scheme shortly afterwards.\n\nThe game is short anyways. You can probably beat it in 45 minutes if you are lucky and use the heavy damage weapons such as the scythe. There is no payoff at the end anyway, a vague poetry slideshow and something about escaping to Mars, before the game loops back to the beginning.",
